        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/problem": "What is the value of $\\frac{2}{3}\\int_{5}^{25}\\frac{3}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right){log}_{5}\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=\\frac{\\log{\\left(x \\right)}}{\\log{\\left(5 \\right)}}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x \\log{\\left(5 \\right)}}\\,\u27f9\\,\\log{\\left(5 \\right)}\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $5$ | $25$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}\\int_{5}^{25}\\frac{3}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right){log}_{5}\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =2\\int_{5}^{25}\\frac{1}{{log}_{5}\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =2\\int_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}5\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =2 \\log{\\left(5 \\right)}\\int_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot\\left(3\\operatorname{ln}5(\\operatorname{ln}Abs(u))\\right)|_{1}^{2} \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot\\left(3\\operatorname{ln}5(\\operatorname{ln}2-\\operatorname{ln}1)\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot\\left(3\\operatorname{ln}2\\operatorname{ln}5\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
